{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Its poles and its sockets.</b> Here חָצֵר is called both in masculine and in feminine — and so in many instances." "<b>And the screen of the gate of the court.</b> A curtain spread along the eastern side, the twenty middle cubits of the width of the court — for it was fifty wide — and it was blocked off from it toward the north fifteen cubits, and likewise toward the south, as it says: ״וַחֲמֵשׁ עֶשְׂרֵה אַמָּה קְלָעִים לַכָּתֵף״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:44.017781664Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}